    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d83">

                <pb facs="0085" n="79" xml:id="pg79"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/6413: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Finland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schoenfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Helsinki</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-20T12:00:00+03:00">August 20,
                            1942—noon.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:49 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>692. Source<anchor n="26" xml:id="d83-f1"/> mentioned in my 691 today<anchor
                        n="27" xml:id="d83-f2"/> confirmed our impressions that Finnish-German trade
                    negotiations just concluded extended German-Finnish grain agreement for another
                    year from September 1 on same terms, namely, 230,000 tons of grain during 12
                    months’ period. This source added that concurrently with commercial negotiations
                    a General of German Army supply service had been in Helsinki and had signed an
                    agreement with Finnish Army supply corps calling for unspecified amount of
                    foodstuffs to be sent for use of Finnish Army. Similar agreements this source
                    said had recently been reached with Hungary and Denmark undoubtedly under German
                    inspiration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schoenfeld</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d83-f1" n="26" xml:id="d83-f1-content">
                <p>A Finnish Army supply officer.</p>
            </note>
